    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "What is the largest 5 digit number divisible by 89?",
      "questionHtml": "What is the largest 5 digit number divisible by 89?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "99911",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">99911</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "99947",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">99947</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "99989",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">99989</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "99999",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">99999</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Largest 5-digit number divisible by 89.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Largest 5-digit number = 99999.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p>When&nbsp;99999 is divided by 89,</p>\n\n<p>=&gt; 99999 = 89 &times; 1123 + 52</p>\n\n<p>Quotient is 1123 and remainder is 52.</p>\n\n<p>Thus, largest 5-digit number which is divisible by 89 = 99999 - 52</p>\n\n<p>= 99947</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700; \">&there4;</span><strong>The answer is 99947.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Find the greatest possible value of (a + b) for which the 8-digit number 143b203a is divisible by 15.",
      "questionHtml": "Find the greatest possible value of (a + b) for which the 8-digit number 143b203a is divisible by 15.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "15",
          "html": "15"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "17",
          "html": "17"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "16",
          "html": "16"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "14",
          "html": "14"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Factors of 15 = (3 × 5)  Hence, the number should be divisible by both 3 and 5.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Possible values of a are 0 and 5,</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, 1 + 4 + 3 + b + 2 + 0 + 3 + 0 =  13 + b, here b can be 2, 5, 8 </p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">For greatest, we need to take 8, so, ( a + b) = ( 0 + 8) = 8, which is not present in the option.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, take a = 5, then 1 +4 +3 +b +2 +0 +3 + 5 = 18 +b, here b can be 0, 3, 6, 9 .</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">For greatest, we need to take b = 9, so, ( a + b) = ( 5 +9 ) = 14, which is in the option as well.</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "If the number 87m6203m is divisible by 6, then find the sum of all possible values ​​of 'm'",
      "questionHtml": "If the number 87m6203m is divisible by 6, then find the sum of all possible values ​​of &#39;m&#39;",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "15",
          "html": "15"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "20",
          "html": "20"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "10",
          "html": "10"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "16",
          "html": "16"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>87m6203m is divisible by 6</p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>If a number is completely divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>If a number ends in a 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8, it is divisible by 2</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Possible values of m could be 0, 2, 4, 6, 8</p>\n\n<p>With 0,</p>\n\n<p>8 + 7 + 0 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 0 = 26 not divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>With 2</p>\n\n<p>8 + 7 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 2 = 30 divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>With 4</p>\n\n<p>8 + 7 + 4 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 4 = 34 not divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>With 6</p>\n\n<p>8 + 7 + 6 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 6 = 38 not divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>With</p>\n\n<p>8 + 7 + 8 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 3 + 8 = 42 divisible by 3</p>\n\n<p>So possible values of m is 2 and 8</p>\n\n<p>So, sum = 10</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4;</strong><strong> Required answer is 10</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "How many two-digit numbers are divisible by 3 or 5?",
      "questionHtml": "How many two-digit numbers are divisible by 3 or 5?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "48",
          "html": "48"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "41",
          "html": "41"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "42",
          "html": "42"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "40",
          "html": "40"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Divisible by 3 <strong>or</strong> 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Using the formula of finding the&nbsp;n<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;term of an AP</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">a<sub>n&nbsp;</sub>= a + (n - 1)&nbsp;&times; d</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The first two-digit number divisible by 3 is 12</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The second two-digit number divisible by 3 is 15</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The third&nbsp;is 18</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">We can see that an AP is formed here, whose first term is 12&nbsp;and the common difference is&nbsp;<strong>3</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">By hit and trial we can find the last two-digit number divisible by 3 will <strong>99, </strong>which<strong>&nbsp;</strong>means&nbsp;the last term of an AP is 99</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><sub><sup>&nbsp;</sup></sub>Here, a = 12&nbsp;, d = 3 and a<sub>n</sub>&nbsp;= 99</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">By putting the values in the formula,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">99 = 12 + (n - 1) <span style=\"\">&times;&nbsp;</span>3</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">n - 1 = 29&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">n = 30</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>The two-digit numbers divisible by 3 are 30</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Similarly, by taking 10 as the first and 95 as the last digit we could find the number of two digit numbers divisible by 5,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; bottom: -0.25em;font-size:10.5px;\"><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Here, a = 10&nbsp;, d = 5&nbsp;and a<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; bottom: -0.25em;font-size:10.5px;\">n</span>&nbsp;= 95</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">By putting the values in the formula,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">95&nbsp;= 10&nbsp;+ (n - 1)&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&times;</span> 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">n - 1 = 17</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">n = 18</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>The&nbsp;two-digit numbers divisible by 5 is 18</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">It is asked in the question that the two-digit number should either be divisible by 3 or 5 but not by both,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The number of two-digit numbers divisible by both can be found by forming AP(Arithmetic progression) as same as&nbsp;above-</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Here, the <strong>first term</strong> and the <strong>common difference</strong> will be <strong>L.C.M.(3 , 5)</strong> i.e. <strong>15</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;By hit and trial, the <strong>last term will be 90</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Using n<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;term formula of an A.P ,&nbsp;<span style=\"\">a</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; bottom: -0.25em; font-size:10.5px;\">n&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">= a + (n +1)&nbsp;&times; d</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;</span>90 = 15 + (n - 1) &times; 15</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">75 =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">(n - 1) &times; 15</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">5 = (n - 1)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>.&middot;. n = 6</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700; \">The two-digit numbers divisible by both 3 and&nbsp;5 are 6.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">So, The total number of two-digit numbers divisible by 3 or 5 will be,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>(Number divisible by 3) + (Number divisible by 5) - (Number divisible by both 3 and 5)</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&rArr;</strong>30 + 18&nbsp;- 6 = 42</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4; The two-digit numbers divisible by 3 or 5 are 42.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "'If N = 9 9 , then N Is divisible by how many positive perfect cubes?",
      "questionHtml": "&#39;If N = 9<sup>9</sup>, then N Is divisible by how many positive perfect cubes?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6",
          "html": "6"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "7",
          "html": "7"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4",
          "html": "4"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "5",
          "html": "5"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>N = 99</p>\n\n<p>N = 3<sup>18</sup></p>\n\n<p>Cubes = 3<sup>0</sup>, 3<sup>3</sup>, 3<sup>6</sup>, 3<sup>9</sup>, 3<sup>12</sup>, 3<sup>15</sup>, 3<sup>18</sup></p>\n\n<p>So, total no. of cubes = 7&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "Find the largest positive integer that will divide 398, 436 and 542 leaving reminders 7, 11 and 15 respectively.",
      "questionHtml": "Find the largest positive integer that will divide 398, 436 and 542 leaving reminders 7, 11 and 15 respectively.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "15",
          "html": "15"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "17",
          "html": "17"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "18",
          "html": "18"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "21",
          "html": "21"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Numbers are 398, 436, and 542 with remainders 7, 11, and 15 respectively.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>To find the largest positive integer that divides multiple numbers leaving specific remainders, we use the formula for the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the differences of the numbers after adjusting for the remainders.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Adjusted numbers:</p>\n\n<p>398 - 7 = 391</p>\n\n<p>436 - 11 = 425</p>\n\n<p>542 - 15 = 527</p>\n\n<p>Now, find the GCD of (391, 425, 527):</p>\n\n<p>391 = 17&nbsp;&times; 23</p>\n\n<p>425 = 17<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&times; 5<sup>2</sup></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">527 = 17&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&times; 31</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">GCD of (391, 425,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">527) is 17.</span></p>\n\n<p>Thus, the largest positive integer that divides 398, 436, and 542 leaving remainders 7, 11, and 15 respectively is 17.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The correct answer is option 2: 17.</strong></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c961fdf51363-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "If (2222) 5555 is divided by 7, the remainder will be _________.",
