lative; width: 0.836em; height: 0px; font-size: 120%;\"><span style=\"position: absolute; clip: rect(1.253em, 1000.84em, 2.562em, -999.997em); top: -2.199em; left: 0em;\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-6310\"><span class=\"semantics\" id=\"MathJax-Span-6311\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-6312\"><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-6313\"><span style=\"font-family: STIXGeneral, &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;, serif; font-size: 83%; font-style: italic; font-weight: normal;\">�</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></nobr><span class=\"MJX_Assistive_MathML\" role=\"presentation\"><span class=\"MathJax\" data-mathml=\"&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot;&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;&amp;#xFFFD;&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;\" id=\"MathJax-Element-78-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><nobr aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-1254\" style=\"width: 1.015em; display: inline-block;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 0.836em; height: 0px; font-size: 120%;\"><span style=\"position: absolute; clip: rect(1.253em, 1000.84em, 2.562em, -999.997em); top: -2.199em; left: 0em;\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-1255\"><span class=\"semantics\" id=\"MathJax-Span-1256\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-1257\"><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-1258\"><span style=\"font-family: STIXGeneral, &quot;Arial Unicode MS&quot;, serif; font-size: 83%; font-style: italic; font-weight: normal;\">�</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></nobr><span class=\"MJX_Assistive_MathML\" role=\"presentation\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>�</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span></span>\n<script id=\"MathJax-Element-78\" type=\"math/mml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>�</mi></mrow></semantics></math></script>\n</span></span> <script id=\"MathJax-Element-343\" type=\"math/mml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>�</mi></mrow></semantics></math></script> </span></span> <script id=\"MathJax-Element-18\" type=\"math/mml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>�</mi></mrow></semantics></math></script> </span></span></span><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);   white-space-collapse: preserve;\"> is a prime number.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);   white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><strong><u>Explanation:</u></strong></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);   white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Let&#39;s find 2222 (mod 7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);   white-space-collapse: preserve;\">We know,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(55, 65, 81);   white-space-collapse: preserve;\">2222 </span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&equiv; 3 (mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">2222<sup>5555&nbsp;</sup>&equiv; 3<sup>5555</sup>&nbsp;(mod 7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, Find 3<sup>5555</sup>(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">3<sup>7</sup><sup>-1</sup></span>&nbsp;compared with <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">fermat&#39;s little theorem a<sup>p-1</sup></span>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">&nbsp;&equiv;1(mod p</span><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">)&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">here, we get&nbsp;7 is prime &nbsp;a = 3 So, </span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">By fermet&#39;s theorem</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">3<sup>6</sup>&equiv;1(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">(3<sup>6</sup>)<sup>925</sup>&equiv;1(mod7</span>)</p>\n\n<p>3<sup>5550</sup><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&equiv;1(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p>3<sup>5555</sup><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&equiv;3<sup>5</sup>(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, 3<sup>5</sup>&equiv;5(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&rArr; 3<sup>5555</sup>&equiv;5(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 2222<sup>5555</sup><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&equiv;5(mod7)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><strong>Hence, OPTION (4) is true</strong></span></p>\n",
