      "id": "c961fdf51363-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "If a three digit number 7X6 is divisible by 11, then the value of X is:",
      "questionHtml": "If a three digit number 7X6 is divisible by 11, then the value of X is:",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "3",
          "html": "3"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2",
          "html": "2"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1",
          "html": "1"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "4",
          "html": "4"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png' width='26px' /> <u style='font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;'>Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Apply the <strong>divisibility rule of 11</strong>: (Sum of digits at odd places) − (Sum of digits at even places) = 0 or 11.</p>\n<p>For the number <strong>7X6</strong>:</p>\n<p>(7 + 6) − X = 11</p>\n<p>13 − X = 11 ⇒ X = 2</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong> The three-digit number is <strong>7X6</strong> and it is <strong>divisible by 11</strong>.</p>\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.testbook.com/tb_solImg_67b6bf92.png/1784026316.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></div>\n<p>According to the <strong>Divisibility Rule of 11</strong>:</p>\n<p>⇒ Sum of digits at <strong>odd places</strong> = 7 + 6 = 13</p>\n<p>⇒ Sum of digits at <strong>even places</strong> = X</p>\n<p>⇒ The difference must be 0 or a multiple of 11 (11, 22, ...).</p>\n<p>⇒ |13 − X| = 0 (Not possible as X would be 13, which is not a single digit)</p>\n<p>⇒ 13 − X = 11</p>\n<p>⇒ X = 13 − 11</p>\n<p>⇒ X = 2</p>\n<p>Thus, the number is <strong>726</strong>. Verification: 726 ÷ 11 = 66. Since the calculation is consistent, <strong>Option (2)</strong> is the correct choice.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 2.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Divisibility Rule of 11</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>A number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of digits at odd places and the sum of digits at even places is 0 or divisible by 11.</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Divisibility Rule of 3</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>A number is divisible by 3 if the <strong>sum of its digits</strong> is divisible by 3.</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Divisibility Rule of 9</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>A number is divisible by 9 if the <strong>sum of its digits</strong> is divisible by 9.</p>\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Single Digit Constraint</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>In any number notation ABC, the placeholders A, B, and C must be <strong>integers from 0 to 9</strong>.</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
