      "solution": "<span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /> <u style=\"font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;\">Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>The <strong>smallest number</strong> divisible by 8, 12, 16, and 20 is their <strong>LCM</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>LCM</strong> (8, 12, 16, 20) = 240.</p>\n<p>To leave a <strong>remainder</strong> of 5, add 5 to the LCM.</p>\n<p>Required Number = 240 + 5 = 245.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 245.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong> Divisors are 8, 12, 16, 20 and the <strong>remainder</strong> is 5.</p>\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong> Required Number = <strong>LCM</strong>(divisors) + <strong>Remainder</strong></p>\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.testbook.com/tb_solImg_c01bea76.png/1784699649.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; width: 420px; max-height: 200px;\"></div>\n<p>Step 1: Find the <strong>Prime Factorization</strong> of the numbers:</p>\n<p>⇒ 8 = 2<sup>3</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ 12 = 2<sup>2</sup> × 3</p>\n<p>⇒ 16 = 2<sup>4</sup></p>\n<p>⇒ 20 = 2<sup>2</sup> × 5</p>\n<p>Step 2: Calculate the <strong>LCM</strong> by taking highest powers:</p>\n<p>⇒ LCM = 2<sup>4</sup> × 3 × 5 = 16 × 15 = 240</p>\n<p>Step 3: Add the constant <strong>remainder</strong>:</p>\n<p>⇒ Smallest number = 240 + 5</p>\n<p>⇒ Smallest number = 245</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 245.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">LCM (Least Common Multiple)</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">The smallest positive integer that is <strong>divisible</strong> by each of the given numbers without leaving a remainder.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Different Remainder Case</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">If remainders (r<sub>1</sub>, r<sub>2</sub>...) are different but (Divisor − Remainder) = k is <strong>constant</strong>, then number = LCM(Divisors) − k.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">HCF Relationship</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">For two numbers A and B: <strong>A × B = LCM(A, B) × HCF(A, B)</strong>.</p>",
      "images": [
