      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /> <u style=\"font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;\">Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Pick the smallest <strong>value</strong> for <strong>x</strong> satisfying the condition: <strong>x</strong> = 6 × 1 + 5 = 11.</p>\n<p>Substitute <strong>x</strong> = 11 into the expression (<strong>x</strong> + 5).</p>\n<p>(11 + 5) = 16.</p>\n<p>Divide 16 by 3 → 16 = 3 × 5 + 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Remainder</strong> = 1.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 1.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.testbook.com/tb_solImg_d74d3ab0.png/1784699121.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; width: 420px; max-height: 200px;\"></div>\n<p><strong>Given:</strong> <strong>x</strong> = 6k + 5, where <strong>k</strong> is an <strong>integer</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>To Find:</strong> <strong>Remainder</strong> of (<strong>x</strong> + 5) ÷ 3.</p>\n<p>⇒ (<strong>x</strong> + 5) = (6k + 5) + 5</p>\n<p>⇒ (<strong>x</strong> + 5) = 6k + 10</p>\n<p>⇒ (<strong>x</strong> + 5) = 3(2k) + (3 × 3 + 1)</p>\n<p>⇒ (<strong>x</strong> + 5) = 3(2k + 3) + 1</p>\n<p>⇒ Since 3(2k + 3) is <strong>exactly divisible</strong> by 3, the <strong>remainder</strong> is 1.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 1.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Euclid's Division Lemma</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">Any <strong>positive integer</strong> a can be written as a = bq + r, where 0 ≤ r < b.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Remainder Addition Rule</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">If <strong>x</strong> leaves <strong>remainder</strong> r<sub>1</sub> when divided by <strong>n</strong>, then (<strong>x</strong> + a) leaves the <strong>remainder</strong> that (r<sub>1</sub> + a) leaves when divided by <strong>n</strong>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Divisibility and Factors</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">If a <strong>number</strong> is <strong>divisible</strong> by 6, it is <strong>automatically divisible</strong> by all <strong>factors</strong> of 6 (i.e., 1, 2, and 3).</p>",
